<hr>
<p>Now let's find the number that belongs at index 1: the second smallest n=
umber. Since index 0 currently contains the smallest value in the array, we=
 won't need to consider index 0 in our search. Therefore, we can find the v=
alue that belongs at index 1 in the range [1, 1 + k]. The smallest value in=
 this range will be the second smallest value overall, which is 4 in this c=
ase.</p>
<p>So, let's swap 4 with the number at index 1 to position 4 as the second =
value in the sorted array:</p>
