<hr>
<p>If we continue this process for the rest of the array, we'll successfull=
y sort the k-sorted array.</p>
<p>The main inefficiency with this approach is finding the minimum number i=
n the range [<code>i</code>, <code>i + k</code>] at each index <code>i</cod=
e>. Linearly searching for it will take <span class=3D"katex"><span class=
=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><seman=
